+Guard 5.5 adds purchase protocol version 3 to the local guard 5.4 source
+including its Sub2 buyer binding and dual-stack guard. The buyer retains
+their native shop token and each paid receipt owns its own subscription,
+effective window, and concurrency tier. Authentication requires an active
+paid window for reusable shop tokens; an ordinary expiry stops access without
+deleting the token. Older machine requests still use their original receipt
+binding. The admin list shows the current tier and retains explicit disable,
+delete, and concurrency overrides. Manual grants remain independent.
+
+The notes below describe the original guard and its operational boundaries.
+For this candidate use the build commands at the end with the updated version.
